A||||2||Ed||Sacramento, California, Sunday Drive||||6||
Z||000000||Ed||04-07-2000||09:59 PM||||The Northern California Chapter of FOCOA is going for a Sunday drive this weekend.  Any board members in this area please e-mail me if you want to join us.<P>We're going to the Sierra foothills' wineries in Amador County, then up the hill a little farther to visit one of our founding members and past president.  <P>Incidentally, it was 83 degrees F. here today.  How's the weather in Wisconsin? <P>||||reg||6
Z||000001||William Federle||04-09-2000||11:57 AM||||It's about 35 deg F outside right now and we<BR>had about 6.5 inches of snow on Friday afternoon and evening. Well, summer can't be too far off - in Wisconsin that's two weeks of rough sledding.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ed||04-09-2000||10:07 PM||||We went for our drive in the beautiful wildflower filled springtime of the foothills of the Sierra. Its cooled off a little to about 75 F.  I have to admit, in a couple of months it will be 105 F and the hills will be brown, but that's in the future.<P>Wine tasting (very moderate intake) was very good.  <P>Big O was able to join us with his supercharged 3.8.  Quite a machine.  <P>I'm hoping to be able to post some pictures in the next couple of days when they come in from a member with a digital camera.  <P>The drive was pretty rapid with only a few holdups, although one CHP (highway patrol officer) gave us a look.  No citations issued. <P>Pictures later (I hope).  ||||reg||1
